## Animation Stack (Priority Order)

1. **CSS + data attributes**: Prefer `tw-animate-css` (already in @packages/ui) with `data-[state=*]` selectors. Use `animate-in`, `animate-out`, `fade-in-0`, `zoom-in-95`, `slide-in-from-*`, `slide-out-to-*` as in shadcn components.
2. **Shadcn built-in**: Use existing component animations (Dialog, Popover, Sheet, Dropdown, etc.)—they already use `data-[state=open]:animate-in data-[state=closed]:animate-out`.
3. **Custom data-driven CSS**: Add `data-*` attributes for state and drive animations via `data-[state=x]:*` or `group-data-[state=x]:*` in Tailwind. Keep it in CSS.
4. **Motion (motion.dev)**: Use only when CSS cannot achieve the effect—drag, scroll-linked animations, layout transitions, gesture-based interactions, shared element transitions. See @.cursor/skills/motion.

**Rule of thumb**: If you can do it with `transition-*` or `animate-*` + data attributes, do not use Motion.

## Spacing Cadence

Use an 8pt-based scale (Tailwind: 1=4px, 2=8px, 4=16px, 6=24px, 8=32px). gap-3 and gap-4 are permitted for component spacing; avoid p-3, p-5, px-5 except for micro-adjustments.

| Level | Classes | Use |
|-------|---------|-----|
| xs | gap-1, p-1 | Badges, icon+text tight |
| sm | gap-2, p-2, space-y-2 | Related inline, label+input |
| md | gap-3, gap-4, p-4, space-y-4 | Component internal, form fields |
| lg | gap-6, p-6, space-y-6 | Section internal, card padding, page sections |
| xl | gap-8, p-8 | Between major blocks |
| 2xl | p-10 | Hero/auth generous layouts |

**Layout**: Main content `p-4 md:p-6`, header `px-4 md:px-6`. Mobile-first. **Forms**: `space-y-2` (label+input), `space-y-4` (between fields), `space-y-6` (between sections).

## Typography Cadence

Use a consistent type scale. Mobile-first: base size on mobile, step up on `md:` for larger screens.

| Level | Classes | Use |
|-------|---------|-----|
| xs | text-xs | Captions, metadata, badges, code snippets |
| sm | text-sm | Body secondary, descriptions, form labels, errors, empty states |
| base | text-base | Body default (implicit) |
| lg | text-lg | Card/section titles |
| xl | text-xl | Page titles (desktop) |
| 2xl | text-2xl | Hero, full-page error titles |

**Page titles**: `text-lg md:text-xl font-heading font-semibold`. **Card titles**: `text-lg font-heading font-semibold`. **Sidebar/panel labels**: `text-sm font-heading font-semibold`. **Body secondary**: `text-sm text-muted-foreground`.

## Design Principles

- **Typography**: Distinctive fonts, avoid generic (Inter, Arial). Pair display + body. See @.cursor/skills/frontend-design.
- **Font usage (dashboard)**: Exception for crypto dashboard theme—Inter (UI) + Poppins (headings).
- **Font classes**: `font-sans` for UI text, `font-heading` / `font-heading font-semibold` for titles and large stats, `numeric` / `tabular-nums` for prices/balances/trading data, `font-mono` for code and API keys.
- **Color & theme**: Semantic tokens from @theme. Dominant colors + sharp accents. Use `bg-primary`, `text-muted-foreground` etc. from design system.
- **Motion**: Purposeful—feedback, orientation, focus. Never decorate. Timing: 100–150ms micro, 200–300ms transitions, 500ms drawers. See @.cursor/skills/emilkowal-animations
- **Easing**: `ease-out` default, `cubic-bezier(0.32, 0.72, 0, 1)` for drawers, springs for natural feel.
- **Properties**: Animate only `transform` and `opacity` for performance. Never `scale(0)`—use min 0.95.

## Accessibility

- Always respect `prefers-reduced-motion`. Use opacity fallback, not full removal. Motion: wrap in `MotionConfig reducedMotion="user"`.

